with the heat wave in the valley the  city of las vegas is reminding pet  owners about a new ordinance  that ordinance cracks down on people who  leave animals under the hot summer sun  hector mejia reports to get the message  across the city of las vegas got  together several agencies  along with a couple of dogs that are  famous on instagram  this year will be hippo the black labs  first time under the hot las vegas sun  make sure she gets air conditioning we  have actually a fan and misters outside  murphy the golden doodle plus this trio  of basset hounds  are helping the local fire department  remind people that it's never a good  idea to leave anyone outside  under extreme heat we experience one to  two calls a day  sometimes even up to 50. there's a new  misdemeanor ordinance in the books to  prevent animal cruelty  chief luis molina is head of the city's  department of public safety  what's changing is that if the  temperatures are expected to seat 105  degrees  and the pet owners are required to  provide misters swamp coolers  air conditioning they cannot leave the  animal in many cases dogs  outside in the heat in addition to that  molina says if the national weather  service sent  out a heat warning animals cannot be  tied outside  they have to be brought in if you see an  unattended pet inside of a hot car  dial 9-1-1 do not try to break into that  car  another reminder that pets can dehydrate  quickly  don't take them for walks during the hot  parts of the day  it's important to know the symptoms of  overheating in pets  which include excessive panting and  difficulty breathing  increased heart and respiratory rate and  drooling and mild weakness stupor and  sometimes and worst case scenarios even  collapse  we'll be posting the specifics on the  changes to the city of las vegas  ordinance on our website  8newsnow.com reporting in downtown  hector mejia  8 news now
 

